language 0.1.0
module network
  means
    Addressing, connectivity and data transfer between network parties,
    including the paths of transfer and the means of applying rules to network
    exchange.

entity network : thing
  means
    network: a bounded area of connectivity within which endpoints can
    exchange data under established rules.

entity endpoint : thing
  means
    endpoint: an addressable party to network exchange.

entity address : thing
  means
    address: a value identifying the location of an endpoint within a definite
    system of network addressing.

entity port : thing
  means
    port: a numeric identifier of a logical point of receiving or sending data
    on a network node, for a definite transport protocol.

entity protocol : thing
  means
    protocol: a set of rules for forming and transferring data between network
    endpoints.

entity connection : thing
  means
    connection: a time-limited context of data exchange between network
    endpoints.

entity route : thing
  means
    route: a rule for choosing the path of network data towards a given
    destination.

entity gateway : thing
  means
    gateway: a network node passing data between different networks or areas
    of connectivity.

entity proxy : thing
  means
    proxy: a network party accepting requests from one party and making
    corresponding requests to another on its own behalf.

entity load-balancer : thing
  means
    load balancer: a network intermediary distributing incoming requests among
    several available recipients.

entity firewall : thing
  means
    firewall: a means of permitting or denying network exchange on the basis
    of given rules.

entity d-n-s-name : thing
  means
    domain name: a hierarchical symbolic name resolved by the domain name
    system into a network address or other data needed for network
    interaction.

entity network-policy : thing
  means
    network policy: a set of normative rules determining admissible network
    connectivity.
